 "about_text": "Richard Heller Gallery is a contemporary art space in Santa Monica, California, run by director and owner Richard Heller with associate director Barry Belkin. Established in 1997, the gallery presents a program centered on figurative and narrative painting, drawing, ceramics, and photography by an international roster of emerging and mid-career artists. Known for supporting artists early in their careers—several of whom went on to significant critical attention—the gallery has built a reputation for eclectic, often humor-inflected exhibitions spanning painting, sculpture, and works on paper. Located at Bergamot Station, the gallery regularly participates in major art fairs and has been the subject of numerous press features on its artists in publications such as the Los Angeles Times, Juxtapoz, and Artillery.",
